{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Betzalel son of Uri son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made all that HaShem commanded</b> — the meaning is that everything was done according to his word, for he was the one who instructed all the wise men, and they all worked before him and showed him all their handiwork, as it says (Exodus 35:34), 'and to teach, He has placed in his heart.' But all the wise-hearted also performed the work, as it says (Exodus 36:8), 'And every wise-hearted one among those doing the work made the Tabernacle.' According to the opinion of our Sages (Jerusalem Talmud, Pe'ah 1:1), this is to his praise, to say that even in matters his teacher did not tell him, his mind concurred with what was stated to Moses from Sinai. The verse did not come to say that he made everything, but rather that he fulfilled in all that was done through him everything that HaShem commanded Moses. Therefore it does not say concerning all that was done up to this point 'as HaShem spoke to Moses,' for that would have implied 'as Moses said by the word of HaShem' — but he (Betzalel) changed the order among them from what Moses had told him. Therefore he included this here to say that he made everything as HaShem said, as I have written above (on 36:8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:13.077230155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}